# ── Secrets: never committed, never published ────────────────────────────────
# This repository is public. A key that reaches a commit is a key that has
# leaked, even if the next commit deletes it: GitHub's secret scanning is
# enabled and its push protection will block the common providers, but the
# first line of defence is this file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.toml
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# ── Internal and client documents: never published ───────────────────────────
# Company, client or internal material stays on the machine it came from.
# Copyrighted industry standards (IOGP, JIP33) are also never redistributed:
# the bundled sample corpus is synthetic markdown written for this repo.
internal/
**/internal/
docs/internal/
*confidential*
*.pdf

# ── Datasets and generated indexes ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything under a demo's data/ is either copyrighted input or a generated
# vector store, and both are rebuilt or supplied locally.
**/data/*
!**/data/.gitkeep

# ── Environments and caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# ── Tooling indexes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.gitnexus/
graphify-out/
.codex/
.agents/
